Introduction
	1. This is the third module of DevOps Pre-requisites training course namely Networking Basics
	2. This module's objective is to introduce fundamental networking concepts which is required for DevOps path.
	3. Module consist of two sections which are "networking basics" and "dns".

Process

	1. Networking Basics: Has three sub-sections
		1.1 Switching
			I. Switch is used for enabling communications between clients which are in the same network.
		1.2 Routing
			I. Router is used for enabling communications between different networks through network tables.
			II. "ip link, ip addr, ip route" are the basic commands to go to
		1.3 Gateway
			I. Gateway is used for sending packets/traffic to the networks we are not directly connected to.
			II. To be able to reach other networks we need to add their gateway to our routing table.
				- These routing table entries should be reciprocal
		1.4 Setting up linux as a router
			I. In linux by default ip forwarding is disabled.
				-To enable it temporarily use "echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward" or "sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1"
				-To enable it permanently change the config file in /etc/sysctl.d/99-ip_forward.conf
		1.5 Lab:
			I. What is the first step of connecting to the internet? -> Having a network interface
			II. We can assign multiple ip addresses to a system
			III. Questions about assigning ip addresses to an interface, viewing routing table, 
			IV. Question about How to add default route.
	2. DNS: Has four sub-sections
		1. Centralizing DNS with a DNS server
			I. Local dns resolve file -> /etc/hosts
			II. Find a remote dns server to resolve -> write nameserver 10.10.10.10 to /etc/resolve.conf
		2. DNS Hierarcyhy and Search Domains
			I. Inspect google.com
				- .com -> top level domain
				- google -> domain name
				- www -> subdomain
			II. write search mycompany.com to /etc/resolve.conf to simplify dns queries. So each time
			some short addresses is used mycompany.com is appended to it.
		3. Common DNS Record Types
			I. How the records are stored in DNS server? Record tables with different types
				-A -> IPv4 address and name matching
				-AAAA -> IPv6 address and name matching
				-CNAME -> domain name and domain name matching.(Used for application with different names)
		4. DNS Diagnostic Tools
			I. To query a domain name we can use nslookup and dig
		5. Lab:
			I. What is dns used for?
			II. Which file is used for dns records on a local linux system
			III. On Linux system, where do we write the dns server information
			IV. Set a dns in the local file
			V. Set dns server for the system
			VI. Top level domain question
			VII. subdomain question
			VIII. Add shortcut for news.yahoo.com so that when we query news, it returns news.yahoo.com
Conclusion

	1. In this module i have revisited fundamental network concepts such as ip address, switching, routing, gateway and dns.
	2. It is essential for any IT role to gain basic insights for how devices communicate with each other
